📌 Time & Space Complexity
Time Complexity  : O(n)
Space Complexity : O(n)
💡 Key Intuition
Water can only be stored if there is a wall on both the left and right.
For every index:
Find the tallest wall on the left.
Find the tallest wall on the right.
The water level is limited by the shorter of these two walls.
Formula:
Water at index i =
min(leftMax[i], rightMax[i]) - height[i]


optimal 
class Solution {
    public int trap(int[] height) {

        // Total number of bars
        int n = height.length;

        // Variable to store total trapped water
        int totalWater = 0;

        // Maximum height seen so far from left and right
        int leftMax = 0;
        int rightMax = 0;

        // Two pointers
        int start = 0;
        int end = n - 1;

        // Traverse until both pointers meet
        while (start < end) {

            // Update maximum heights from both sides
            leftMax = Math.max(leftMax, height[start]);
            rightMax = Math.max(rightMax, height[end]);

            // Process the side with the smaller maximum wall
            if (leftMax <= rightMax) {

                // Water trapped at current left index
                totalWater += leftMax - height[start];

                // Move left pointer
                start++;

            } else {

                // Water trapped at current right index
                totalWater += rightMax - height[end];

                // Move right pointer
                end--;
            }
        }

        return totalWater;
    }
}
